{"content":[{"c":["PATHROS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["The region of Upper Egypt, mentioned five times in the Hebrew OT (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.11.11","r":"Isa.11.11","rawR":"Isa.11.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.11.11","value":"Isa.11.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 11:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.44.1,15","r":"Jer.44.1,15","rawR":"Jer.44.1,15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.44.1,15","value":"Jer.44.1,15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 44:1, 15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.29.14","r":"Ezek.29.14","rawR":"Ezek.29.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.29.14","value":"Ezek.29.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 29:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.30.14","r":"Ezek.30.14","rawR":"Ezek.30.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.30.14","value":"Ezek.30.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"30:14"},"). Each time it occurs in conjunction with a city in Lower Egypt (Noph = Memphis, or Zoan = Tanis). The Hebrew is ",{"c":["Pathros"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," and the Egyptian is ",{"c":["pa to resy"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," (“the Southern Land”). Egyptologists believe that the Hebrew form is a corruption of ",{"c":["Pethoris"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," or ",{"c":["Pethores."],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.11.11","r":"Isa.11.11","rawR":"Isa.11.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.11.11","value":"Isa.11.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isaiah 11:11"}," suggests that ",{"c":["Mitsrayim"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"}," is to be equated with Lower and Middle Egypt, and ",{"c":["Pathros"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"}," is the region south of it up to the border of Cush (i.e., Upper Egypt). According to ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.29.14","r":"Ezek.29.14","rawR":"Ezek.29.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.29.14","value":"Ezek.29.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezekiel 29:14"},", Pathros is the original home of the Egyptians. The prophets spoke about God’s judgment on Pathros: “I will lay waste Upper Egypt [“Pathros,” mg], set fire to Zoan and inflict punishment on Thebes” (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.30.14","r":"Ezek.30.14","rawR":"Ezek.30.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.30.14","value":"Ezek.30.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 30:14"},", ",{"c":["niv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). After the exile, Jews migrated to Egypt and some settled in Pathros. Jeremiah warned that God’s judgment on Egypt was to come and that they would not escape it: “This word came to Jeremiah concerning all the Jews living in Lower Egypt—in Migdol, Tahpanhes and Memphis—and in Upper Egypt [Pathros]: ‘This is what the ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"divine-name","t":"span"}," Almighty, the God of Israel, says: You saw the great disaster I brought on Jerusalem and on all the towns of Judah. Today they lie deserted and in ruins’ ” (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.44.1-2","r":"Jer.44.1-2","rawR":"Jer.44.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.44.1-2","value":"Jer.44.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 44:1-2"},", ",{"c":["niv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Pathros","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Is 11:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.11.11","rawQueryValue":"Isa.11.11","sourceRefExact":"Isa.11.11"},{"anchorText":"Jer 44:1, 15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.44.1,15","rawQueryValue":"Jer.44.1,15","sourceRefExact":"Jer.44.1,15"},{"anchorText":"Ez 29:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.29.14","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.29.14","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.29.14"},{"anchorText":"30:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.30.14","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.30.14","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.30.14"},{"anchorText":"Isaiah 11:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.11.11","rawQueryValue":"Isa.11.11","sourceRefExact":"Isa.11.11"},{"anchorText":"Ezekiel 29:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.29.14","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.29.14","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.29.14"},{"anchorText":"Ez 30:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.30.14","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.30.14","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.30.14"},{"anchorText":"Jer 44:1-2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.44.1-2","rawQueryValue":"Jer.44.1-2","sourceRefExact":"Jer.44.1-2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0a3d0f8a7587567905b8c01277e1a02255a5fb7931e97b440aeb9e720042d7aa","sourceItemName":"Pathros","sourceItemOrder":62,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Pathros","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Pathros","title":"Pathros","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}